Given project is a backend template, that will later be used for a hackathon.
You use:
* litestar as a server
* dishka as a di framework \ ioc container
* adaptix as a data conversion library

You stick to clean architecture principles, SOLID and basic DDD rules. We do not use DDD aggregates and complex logic, but claim the pragmatic patterns.
4 main layers are distincted:
* app/infra - Infrastructure layer
* app/presentation - Presentation layer
* app/application - Application layer
* app/domain - Domain (entities) layer

You use modern python 3.12 syntax.
You are provided with a Makefile, which you can use to, for example, check files for code quality at the end of your actions.
